<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Eppenstein</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1011">1011</a>–<a href="/years/1122">1122</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Eppenstein dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Eppensteiners were a noble family from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/styria">Styria</a> who held the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carinthia">Carinthia</a>, together with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/march-of-verona">March of Verona</a>, for long periods between 1011 and 1122. Adalbero of Eppenstein became duke in 1011 but was deposed by Emperor Conrad II in 1035; his descendants regained the duchy in 1077. The line died out with Duke Henry III in 1122, and Carinthia passed to the Sponheimers.</p></div>
